  "/guides/office-deep-cleaning-checklist/": {
    "title": "Office Deep Cleaning Checklist Before Booking | Deepcleaning99",
    "description": "Prepare an office-cleaning enquiry with floor area, washrooms, carpets, access hours and equipment instructions for a clearer quotation.",
    "eyebrow": "DEEPCLEANING99",
    "h1": "What an office deep cleaning quote should cover",
    "heroP": "",
    "crumbs": "Home / Article three",
    "proseHtml": "<p>Two offices with the same floor area can need very different amounts of work. One may have open desks and hard flooring. Another may have several washrooms, carpets, upholstered seating and a busy pantry.</p><p>Begin your enquiry with a list of areas. Include workstations, floors, accessible glass, doors, pantry and washrooms. State whether carpets need shampooing or sofas need fabric cleaning; those services should appear explicitly in the quote.</p><p>Share photographs and fixture counts. For washrooms, the number of toilets, urinals and basins helps describe the job. For the pantry, mention grease buildup and which cabinets will be emptied. Tell the cleaning team about delicate surfaces or any equipment that cannot be moved.</p><p>Agree on access. If the team needs to work after office hours, arrange security permission and a person who can open the premises. Confirm water, power and the permitted lift or loading route. Confidential records and staff belongings should be secured before the visit.</p><p>Check reopening requirements. Carpet or upholstery cleaning may need drying time. If staff must return by a set hour, discuss that condition before approving the work.</p><p>For a recurring arrangement, write down the cleaning checklist and number of visits. A quarterly deep clean is not the same service as daily housekeeping. A clear quote makes the difference visible and gives both sides a practical checklist to review after the work.</p><p>Related links: Office Deep Cleaning / Commercial Cleaning / Cleaning AMC</p>",
    "faqs": [],
    "dataService": "Office Deep Cleaning",
    "aside": {
      "h": "A clear quote. A suitable slot.",
      "p": "Share your property size, photographs and preferred appointment."
    },
    "cards": []
  },
  "/guides/prepare-home-for-deep-cleaning/": {
    "title": "How to Prepare Your Home for Deep Cleaning | Deepcleaning99",
    "description": "A practical checklist for clearing cupboards, arranging access and planning upholstery drying before a home deep-cleaning appointment.",
    "eyebrow": "DEEPCLEANING99",
    "h1": "How to prepare your home for a deep cleaning visit",
    "heroP": "",
    "crumbs": "Home / Article one",
    "proseHtml": "<p>You do not need to clean the house before the cleaners arrive. What helps is giving the team access to the work you have booked.</p><p>Start with the booking summary. If cupboard interiors are included, empty those cupboards. If sofa cleaning is booked, clear the seats and nearby floor space. A full-home booking does not automatically cover everything inside every drawer or cupboard.</p><p>Put jewellery, cash, important papers and fragile items away. Tell the team about loose taps, cracked tiles, delicate stone, recently painted surfaces or furniture that should not be moved. These details are easier to manage before work begins.</p><p>Arrange water, electricity and building access. If the society needs advance permission, a gate entry or a service lift booking, sort that out before the appointment. Share the correct flat number and a contact who can answer the team’s call.</p><p>Plan around upholstery drying. A cleaned sofa or mattress may need to remain unused for some time. Ask about the likely method and drying requirements rather than assuming it will be ready straight away. Keep the room ventilated and follow the advice given after cleaning.</p><p>For move-in jobs, the simplest arrangement is often to clean after renovation is finished and before unpacking. If cement residue or paint marks remain, send photographs first so the team can assess them separately.</p><p>Before the team leaves, check the agreed areas together. Point out anything that needs another look while the equipment is still on site.</p><p>Related links: Full Home Deep Cleaning / Sofa Cleaning / Service Quality</p>",
    "faqs": [],
    "dataService": null,
    "aside": {
      "h": "A clear quote. A suitable slot.",
      "p": "Share your property size, photographs and preferred appointment."
    },
    "cards": []
  },
  "/guides/sofa-cleaning-drying-and-stains/": {
    "title": "Sofa Cleaning Drying Time and Stain Expectations | Deepcleaning99",
    "description": "Understand why sofa material, ventilation and existing stains affect cleaning methods, drying and results before booking a service.",
    "eyebrow": "DEEPCLEANING99",
    "h1": "What to check before booking sofa cleaning",
    "heroP": "",
    "crumbs": "Home / Article two",
    "proseHtml": "<p>The seat count is useful for a quotation, but the material matters for the cleaning itself. Fabric, leather and delicate upholstery cannot all be treated in the same way.</p><p>Look for a care label and share it if available. Send a photograph of the sofa and any marks that concern you. Mention previous colour bleeding, a damaged seam or a stain that has already been treated with a household product. An L-shaped sofa may also need its chaise measured as seat-equivalents.</p><p>Ask what is included. Some bookings cover the seats, backs and armrests but price loose cushions separately. Confirm those items before the appointment so there is no confusion at the property.</p><p>Allow time for drying. The method, fabric, room airflow and weather all affect how quickly upholstery dries. More water does not automatically mean a better clean. The team should select a compatible process and advise you when the sofa can be used.</p><p>Finally, keep stain expectations realistic. Dirt and removable marks are different from faded colour, dye transfer or worn fabric. Cleaning may improve an old mark without removing it completely. It cannot repair the material underneath.</p><p>Choose an appointment when the sofa can be left unused for the necessary period. Keep children and pets away while the work is happening, and avoid covering damp upholstery.</p><p>Related links: Sofa Cleaning / Carpet Cleaning / Booking FAQs</p>",
    "faqs": [],
    "dataService": "Sofa Cleaning",
    "aside": {
      "h": "A clear quote. A suitable slot.",
      "p": "Share your property size, photographs and preferred appointment."
    },
    "cards": []
  },
