    "proseHtml": "<p>Grease collects near the stove, along cabinet edges and on the tiles behind the cooking area. A quick surface wipe may leave the sticky layer underneath. Our kitchen service focuses on the accessible areas included in your booking.</p><p>Tell us whether the kitchen is occupied or empty, its approximate size and how long it has been since a detailed clean. Photographs help us judge heavy grease before sending the team.</p><h2>Included areas</h2><p>The agreed scope can include the countertop, sink, hob exterior, accessible wall tiles, floor, cabinet exteriors and reachable grease. Cabinet interiors can be cleaned when they are empty and included in the quotation. We choose products according to the surface and test delicate finishes before cleaning.</p><p>Utensil washing, chimney dismantling, duct work, grease traps, appliance repairs and appliance interiors are separate from a standard kitchen package. Please mention them if they are part of your requirement.</p><h2>Getting the kitchen ready</h2><p>Remove food, utensils and stored items from cupboards that need internal cleaning. Let the hob cool down. Keep access to water and power available. If you need help moving and replacing utensils, ask for a separate quote rather than assuming it is included.</p><h2>Kitchen questions</h2><details><summary>Will all grease come off?</summary><p>Removable grease is the aim, but old damage, discolouration or a worn coating may remain after cleaning.</p></details><details><summary>Do you clean restaurant kitchens?</summary><p>Yes, with a commercial scope. Share the kitchen area, operating hours and photographs so we can assess it.</p></details><details><summary>Can this be booked regularly?</summary><p>Yes. Scheduled kitchen cleaning can be arranged for an agreed frequency and scope.</p></details>",
