    "heroP": "",
    "crumbs": "Home / Sofa cleaning",
    "proseHtml": "<p>A sofa can look tidy while holding dust in the fabric, seams and spaces between cushions. Food marks and spills also need attention, but the right cleaning method depends on the upholstery.</p><p>Tell us the number of seats and whether the sofa is fabric or leather. For an L-shaped sofa or chaise, send a photograph so we can confirm the seat-equivalent count. Loose cushion cleaning should be added separately where it is not included.</p><h2>How fabric sofas are cleaned</h2><p>We inspect the material and condition, check available care instructions and test a small area. Suitable fabric can be vacuumed, treated for selected marks and cleaned with an appropriate shampoo or extraction method. Backs and armrests are included where stated in your package.</p><p>Leather sofas need leather-specific cleaning. We do not treat leather as ordinary fabric or use wet extraction on it.</p><h2>Drying and stain expectations</h2><p>Drying depends on the material, moisture used, room ventilation and weather. Plan the visit when the sofa can remain unused for the drying period advised by the team. Avoid covering damp upholstery with sheets or plastic.</p><p>Old stains, dye transfer, faded fabric and wear may remain. We cannot promise that every mark will disappear or that cleaning will restore damaged upholstery.</p><h2>Sofa questions</h2><details><summary>Is the rate per sofa or per seat?</summary><p>Standard sofas are usually quoted by seat count, with a minimum booking amount. Check your summary for the final price.</p></details><details><summary>Are detachable cushions included?</summary><p>Only if the package includes them or you add them to the booking.</p></details><details><summary>Can you clean office lounge sofas?</summary><p>Yes. Send the total seat count and material details for a commercial quote.</p></details>",
